            "highlight_color": "#000000",
            "highlight_text_color": "",
            "spacing_bottom": 12
          }
        },
        "text_DEbVYc": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>Each idiom fragrance expresses one focused idea. An ingredient, a note, or a thought.</p><p>Everything else is there to frame, support and complement it. Backing singers, if you</p><p>like. We call them single-minded fragrances.</p><p>This clarity is what makes idiom fragrances great for layering.</p><p>It sounds easy. But it means there is nowhere to hide. *Just ask Oscar W. Or was it Mark T.</p><p>Our ideas come from curiosity - about the world, the wacky people in it, and the</p><p>extraordinary palette of materials found in nature and chemistry. The new is out there,</p><p>just unassembled.</p><p>Then we refine, debate and test our ideas on whoever we can find. A lot. Getting</p><p>through a forest of smelling strips along the way. Until we find that elusive combination</p><p>of clarity, character and, dare we say it, soul that makes an idiom fragrance.</p>",
            "size": 100,
            "text_position": "left",
            "spacing_bottom": 12
          }
        },
